\tag{fdip}
\title{Ultrametric coarse-graining}
\date{2026-11-03}

\p{Can the law on a coarser grid be recovered exactly from the law on
a finer grid?}

\p{Pair averages of a nearest-neighbour Gaussian on a path of 6
vertices are not nearest-neighbour: the two end blocks acquire a
positive precision entry. The following section diagonalizes a
precision built from nested residue classes. The next section takes
up the means of those classes. A further section records a common
fourth moment.}

